      "scenes": [
        {
          "audio": "Let's first talk about the difference between open source and closed source.",
          "label": "Opening Hook",
          "visual": "A white retro flip clock against a solid black background. The numbers '00' are displayed in a bold sans-serif font. The clock flip animation is fast and smooth. The lighting is uniform across the graphic elements.",
          "shot_type": "Medium Shot",
          "scene_number": 1,
          "timestamp_end": "0:01",
          "timestamp_start": "0:00"
        },
        {
          "audio": "Part one: Open source and closed source.",
          "label": "Product Information",
          "visual": "The flip clock changes to '01'. Below the clock, stylized text elements appear in white, grey, and bold pink accents. The background remains solid black.",
          "shot_type": "Medium Shot",
          "scene_number": 2,
          "timestamp_end": "0:02",
          "timestamp_start": "0:01"
        },
        {
          "audio": "Closed source is a bit like going to a restaurant to eat. The food is delicious, right?",
          "label": "Usage Scenarios",
          "visual": "The background switches to solid white. A series of flat icons appear: a silver cloche with steam rising, a rounded rectangle containing the cloche icon with a checkmark. Soft, subtle drop shadows are used under the white cards. The color palette is primarily black, white, and light grey.",
          "shot_type": "Medium Shot",
          "scene_number": 3,
          "timestamp_end": "0:05",
          "timestamp_start": "0:02"
        },
        {
          "audio": "But the kitchen is with someone else. You can only order food and pay by the portion. You can't get the recipe.",
          "label": "Problem Solving",
          "visual": "New icons slide into view: a chef's hat representing the kitchen and a notepad representing a menu. A lock icon appears on the menu. A cursor moves across the screen to click on menu items, which highlights them in purple. An 'X' icon appears over the recipe card.",
          "shot_type": "Medium Shot",
          "scene_number": 4,
          "timestamp_end": "0:10",
          "timestamp_start": "0:05"
        },
        {
          "audio": "Open source means someone just made the recipe public. You can download the model file and run it on your own machine. Use it however you want.",
          "label": "Product Selling Points",
          "visual": "The screen transitions to show an open lock icon next to a document. Icons of a file named 'JEV-27B' and a computer server appear. An arrow shows a download process moving a file to the server. The server icon then shows a green status dot with a pulsating ring to indicate it is running. The design is clean, using a high-contrast black and white theme with purple accents.",
          "shot_type": "Medium Shot",
          "scene_number": 5,
          "timestamp_end": "0:17",
          "timestamp_start": "0:10"
        }
      ]
